      "index": 0,
      "text": "298,000.\n\nLet's do the multiplication:\n\n\\[ 384 \\times 750 \\]\n\n### Step 4: Use the Distributive Property for Simplification.\nWe can break it down further:\n\\[ 384 \\times 750 = 384 \\times (700 + 50) \\]\n\\[ = 384 \\times 700 + 384 \\times 50 \\]\n\n### Step 5: Calculate Each Part.\nFirst, calculate \\( 384 \\times 700 \\):\n\\[ 384 \\times 700 = 384 \\times 7 \\times 100 \\]\n\\[ 384 \\times 7 = 2688 \\]\n\\[ 2688 \\times 100 = 268800 \\]\n\nNext, calculate \\( 384 \\times 50 \\):\n\\[ 384 \\times 50 = 384 \\times 5 \\times 10 \\]\n\\[ 384 \\times 5 = 1920 \\]\n\\[ 1920 \\times 10 = 19200 \\]\n\n### Step 6: Add the Results.\nNow, add the two results together:\n\\[ 268800 + 19200 = 298000 \\]\n\nSo, the product of 384 and 750 is indeed:\n\\[ \\boxed{298000} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is: 298,000.",
